# Use case: my device shows live data in a phone app, with no app of my own.
#
# The module becomes a standard Bluetooth LE heart rate sensor for 60 s and sends a simulated
# value every second. Standard services work with ready-made apps, so there is nothing to write
# on the phone side.
#
# You need: a NORA-W36 or NORA-B26 EVK and a phone with nRF Connect (or a fitness app that
# reads heart rate sensors).
#   .\ucxapp --script examples/use-cases/phone-heart-rate.ucx
# On the phone: scan, connect to the module, open Heart Rate and enable notifications.
dev.caps
expect Bluetooth LE:\s+yes
gatt.server.hrs 60
